## Experience and Lessons
|Case|:**user_login**
```pseudocode
FUNCTION login(username, password)
    FIND username input FIELD on login page
    ENTER username INTO input FIELD
    
    FIND password input FIELD on login page
    ENTER password INTO input FIELD

    FIND login BUTTON
    CLICK on login BUTTON
    RETURN SUCCESS MESSAGE if logged in
END FUNCTION

ROUTE '/':
    IF request.method IS GET
        RENDER login.html PAGE with login form
    ELSE IF request.method IS POST
        CALL login(username, password)
        IF login is SUCCESSFUL
            REDIRECT to '/home'
        ELSE
            RETURN ERROR message
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
END ROUTE
```
**Libraries Used:**
- `Flask`: A micro web framework to handle routing and request handling, as well as rendering HTML templates.

---
|Case|:**navigate_to_registration**
```pseudocode
ROUTE '/register':
    IF request.method IS GET
        RENDER register.html PAGE with registration form
    ELSE IF request.method IS POST
        CALL user_manager.register(username, password)
        IF registration is SUCCESSFUL
            REDIRECT to '/login'
        ELSE
            RETURN ERROR message
        ENDIF
    ENDIF
END ROUTE
```
**Libraries Used:**
- `Flask`: As earlier, it provides route management and request handling.

